Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.8.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.8.0 fixes the three defects seen on device in 0.7.0 (archive #7), where the picture finally appeared but was wrong and route 4 crashed SpringBoard into safe mode. (1) WRONG ASPECT RATIO on route 3: the presentation view's natural size equals scene.settings.frame, but a real app scene is full-screen (430x932, ratio 0.461) while the floating window content area is 267x336.6 (ratio 0.793), so the hosted content was stretched. Route 4 looked correct precisely because it baked frame = contentArea.bounds into the scene at creation. 0.8.0 therefore defaults hostSceneFrame to true: the scene frame is set to the content-area size before presenting, re-synced 3 s later (updateSettingsWithBlock: is asynchronous) and re-applied whenever the user resizes the window with the corner grip. (2) SAFE MODE from route 4: crash attribution was crashedStep=P4-scene and MF-host-step-prev.txt stopped at ">>> P4-scene" - the same SpringBoard pid called createSceneWithDefinition: a SECOND time with the SAME scene identity (com.apple.mobilesafari-multifloat), and FBSceneManager asserts on a duplicate identity. The own scene is now acquired through MFAcquireOwnSceneForApp: reuse the live one if it belongs to the same app, otherwise look it up with FBSceneManager -sceneWithIdentifier: and ADOPT it, otherwise destroy the stale one with destroyScene:withTransitionContext: (using a real FBScene -_createTransitionContext, never nil), and a hard cap of one creation per app per process. The config migration also moves hostRoute 4 -> 3 once, since 4 crashed SpringBoard. (3) SILENT BLACK FALLBACK: every retry logged "createPresenter 抛异常: Cannot create a presenter with this identifier as it's already in use." and the old code then silently mounted the known-black SBDeviceApplicationSceneViewController, so a retry looked like the picture turning black. Presenters are now reused when scene+identifier match (activate re-issued as needed), torn down (deactivate + invalidate) when the target changes, and a presenter failure no longer falls back to route B unless allowRouteB=true is set explicitly. Config, all defaults can be overridden in /var/mobile/MultiFloat.plist: hostRoute 3 (3 = adopt the existing scene, 4 = build our own - now guarded), hostSceneFrame true, resizesHosted true, forceForeground true, allowRouteB false, hostStep 6. Config structure version cfgVersion=8, migrated once on first launch. DISABLED BY DEFAULT for real hosting: needs enabled=true AND hostEnabled=true. Crash-guard marker still makes a crash loop impossible. No hooks are installed. Log: /var/mobile/MultiFloat.log
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
